    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0616" n="330" xml:id="pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2069</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-10T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2686. Department’s 2599, December 18.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d446-f1"/> Conditions
                    enforced by British authorities in China are causing great damage to American
                    trade. Bring matter again to attention Foreign Office and urge early reply.
                    Further and increasingly pressing complaints are being received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
